From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: Let JSON.parse and String.prototype.split take interrupts, and
 throw instead of ending the process past the largest array

JSON.parse only checked for stack overflow: a termination requested while
it parses (a CPU or memory limit of the embedder) took effect only after
the whole text, however much it allocated meanwhile. Handle interrupts
once per value, as JSON.stringify does. String.prototype.split creates
every part in one runtime call; handle interrupts every 1,024 parts.

A JSON array or a split with more elements than FixedArray::kMaxLength,
and a JSON object with more properties than its dictionary can hold,
ended the process ("Fatal JavaScript invalid size error", "invalid array
length", "invalid table size"), reachable from a script with one text of
a few hundred megabytes. Throw a RangeError instead (Invalid array length,
Too many properties to enumerate). The split stops collecting indices one
past the maximum.

